Expected elements: REPLACED — "A timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace" by the bare `128 / 1315` fraction readout in the identity bar

Everything else required is present: banner, exit to `aztec`, truncated hash, `Partial`, block, both stepping directions, phase rail, Code positioned at line 32, Call Trace / Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open, Values as a separate pane, Transaction identity. Nothing forbidden. But no time surface renders at 1440, so finding 1 is P1 and the rating is capped at 4.

This dark theme is designed, not inverted: three real surface levels, an editor-grade syntax palette, and — this round's win — position is cyan, changed is amber, navigation keeps indigo, and the open tab drops hue for a neutral underline. Line 32 and the selected frame share one position treatment across panes: B5 passing.

What remains is that amber now carries two meanings, and that the theme's quiet end is too quiet. The line-number gutter, the inline annotation chips, the inactive phase chips and the Transaction pane's explanatory sentence all sit under the small-text contrast floor, and the stepping buttons show no disabled treatment while the rail says the engine is still fetching — so colour is not carrying one of the three things the spec makes it carry.

Highest-priority fixes: separate the outcome badge from the diff amber; lift the gutter and the annotation chips off the floor.

Rating: 4/10

